 is properly grounded, it protects against electrical faults and surges that could otherwise disrupt network operations or damage sensitive equipment, leading to security vulnerabilities. Therefore, the physical infrastructure of cable management systems directly impacts the digital security of the network. [Data: Entities (8, 102, 85, 93), Relationships (111)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The Role of Grounding in Ensuring Network Reliability\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Grounding is not only a safety measure but also a critical factor in ensuring the reliable operation of network equipment. Electrical grounding helps to prevent electromagnetic interference (EMI) and radio frequency interference (RFI), which can disrupt data transmission and compromise network performance. By providing a path for stray electrical currents to dissipate safely, grounding systems ensure that equipment operates within its intended parameters. This is particularly important in complex network environments where multiple devices communicate with each other. The integration of grounding into cable management solutions like BANDEJAS and DUTOS ensures that this reliability is built into the physical infrastructure. [Data: Entities (8, 102, 85)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the direct correlation between proper grounding, infrastructure standards, and overall network security, indicating significant potential for disruption or compromise if these elements are neglected.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "STOP"}}], "created": 1788041285, "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": "default", "system_fingerprint"